{
  "id": "ss.relic.growth",
  "name": "Rootstock",
  "description": "A cut trunk and everything under it: five primary roots off the collar, six finer ones splitting away from those, and the grain still showing on the shaft. All of the body is below the line \u2014 which is the half of taking root that a spore or a leaf never shows. Polish: every root now sits on its own ink underlay \u2014 the six finer ones had none and were a pixel wide, so they are half again as thick \u2014 the stock has a lit left face and a shaded right side in place of the hairline grain lines, and each primary root carries a dark underside. The ink in the root zone is deliberately lighter than on the stock: the roots sit three to five pixels apart, and full-weight ink fused the fingers into a skirt in silhouette. Five roots, six branches, the same spread.",
  "tags": ["relic"],
  "says": ["finds"],
  "size": [32, 32],
